**/*
!/RUNTIMES.md
!/**/*.ts
!/**/*.js
!/**/*.mjs
!/package.json
!/jsr.json
!/dist/**/*.json
!/esm/**/*.json
!/**/*.map

# The QM deployment-layer bundle. `pipeshub init-qm` reads these out of the
# installed package, so they must ship. This file is an allowlist — everything
# is excluded by the `**/*` above — and the bundle is .json, .md, .jsonc and a
# Dockerfile, none of which the rules above re-include.
!/qm/**

# ...except qm/docs/, which is for this repository, not for the package.
# It holds a draft of a docs-site page and an ADR draft marked "not for
# filing". Neither is read by `init-qm`, and shipping internal drafts to every
# operator who installs the CLI is not something to do by accident.
/qm/docs

/eslint.config.mjs
/__tests__
